# Cache and security headers.
#
# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages read this verbatim. Vercel reads `vercel.json`
# instead — see the `headers` array there, which mirrors this file rule for rule.
# nginx and Apache have no repo config; docs/10-DEPLOY.md § Host configuration
# has the equivalents.
#
# THE ONE LINE THAT IS NOT OPTIONAL
# The SPA rewrite in `_redirects`. Without it, refreshing /rankings or
# /school/16 returns a 404 from the host, because the only HTML file on disk is
# index.html. This is a client-routed site: three real files, 46 reachable URLs.
#
# THE ORDERING MATTERS AND IS PROVED, NOT ASSUMED
# Netlify applies the FIRST matching rule, so the specific rules come first and
# the catch-all comes last. That is the opposite of how a naive reading of
# "most specific wins" would order them, so it is worth stating.
#
# After deploying, confirm with:
#   curl -sI https://your-domain/           | grep -i cache-control  # no-cache
#   curl -sI https://your-domain/assets/…js | grep -i cache-control  # immutable
# If the second says no-cache, the order below is wrong for your host.

# Fingerprinted by Vite from a content hash, so the URL changes whenever the
# bytes do. Safe to cache forever.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# NOT fingerprinted. Vite copies public/ verbatim, so these URLs are stable even
# if the bytes change — which means `immutable` here would pin returning visitors
# to a stale font for a year after anyone re-ran `npm run fonts`.
# Revalidated weekly instead: a week of free repeat loads, and a changed font
// reaches people within a week rather than never.
# The real fix is to fingerprint them, which means moving them out of public/ —
# see docs/10-DEPLOY.md § The font cache trap.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, must-revalidate
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# The document must never be cached, or a deploy is invisible to anyone already
# holding a copy. no-cache means "revalidate", not "don't store".
#
# This is a catch-all rather than a rule for /index.html, and that is the whole
# point. A reader requests `/` or `/rankings`, not `/index.html` — so a rule
# scoped to the filename matches the one URL nobody asks for, and the URL that
# matters falls through to the host default, which on most CDNs is cacheable.
# The catch-all has to come AFTER /assets and /fonts so those keep their
# long-lived caching.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()

# No Content-Security-Policy, on purpose. The 2-second splash, the 3-4s ranking
# chunk and the font set are not security-sensitive, and there is no user input,
# no cookies and no third-party origin on this site. A wrong CSP is the fastest
# way to break a working deploy, and a strict one buys almost nothing here.
# If one is added later, `default-src 'self'` is the correct baseline: every
# value in this repo is same-origin, so nothing else needs allowing.
